# Vue Frontend Rules

## Stack

- Vue 3 with Composition API and `<script setup lang="ts">`
- Vite + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Pinia for state management

## Structure

```
frontend/src/
├── components/     # Reusable UI components
├── composables/    # Shared logic (useAuth, useProjects, etc.)
├── views/          # Route-level pages
├── stores/         # Pinia stores
└── api/            # API client functions
```

## Standards

- Extract reusable logic into composables
- Keep components under 200 lines — split if larger
- Use TypeScript interfaces for API response types
- No secret values stored in client state beyond display needs
- Handle loading and error states in every data-fetching view

## API Calls

- Centralize HTTP calls in `src/api/`
- Use composables to wrap API calls with loading/error state
- Never hardcode tokens — use session/auth store
